+*   **Strengths:** Significantly enhances specular view-dependent effects compared to standard 3DGS, particularly on shiny/reflective surfaces [S1]. Maintains rapid training and rendering speeds due to the compact tensorial representation and rasterization pipeline [S1].
+*   **Limitations:** Requires additional optimization of BRDF features and a neural network, increasing complexity over vanilla 3DGS. Performance on complex real-world scenes (Tanks and Temples) is superior to 3DGS but may not match dedicated neural radiance field methods in all metrics [S1].
